  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0078 database is designed to track financial transactions and billing information for various entities. At its core is the billable table, which stores information about each entity, including the processor used, processor ID, trial end date, card type, last four digits of the card number, expiration month and year, and any extra billing information. The pay_charges table is used to record individual charges, with each charge having a unique ID, owner type, owner ID referencing the billable entity, processor, processor ID, amount, amount refunded, card type, last four digits of the card number, expiration month and year, and timestamps for creation and update. The pay_subscriptions table stores subscription information, including the owner ID referencing the billable entity, subscription name, processor, processor ID, processor plan, quantity, trial end date, end date, status, and timestamps for creation and update. The pay_charges and pay_subscriptions tables both reference the billable table, establishing a relationship between charges and subscriptions.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a payments engine specifically designed for Ruby on Rails (version 6.0 and higher), aimed at managing payments and subscriptions. It integrates with several payment processors including Stripe, Paddle, Braintree, and Lemon Squeezy, with additional support for a fake processor for testing purposes.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to facilitate secure and efficient handling of payment transactions and managing subscriptions across multiple processors. The system must support Strong Customer Authentication (SCA) and accommodate payments via credit card and PayPal where applicable.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- End Users: Individuals or businesses using the Ruby on Rails application who require subscription management and payment processing.\n- Developers: Ruby on Rails developers integrating the payment engine into their applications.\n- Administrators: Personnel responsible for overseeing payment processing and managing subscriptions.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Payment Processing:\n   - Integrate with supported processors: Stripe, Paddle, Braintree, Lemon Squeezy, and a fake processor for testing.\n   - Handle payment transactions securely using current SCA protocols.\n   - Support PayPal payments where applicable.\n\n2. Subscription Management:\n   - Create, update, and terminate subscriptions.\n   - Track subscription details, including plan type, quantity, and status.\n   - Manage trial periods and subscription end dates.\n\n3. Transaction Tracking:\n   - Record detailed information about each transaction, including amount, refund status, and payment method details.\n   - Store and update transactional data securely.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- The system must be compatible with Ruby on Rails 6.0 and higher.\n- Ensure data security and integrity in line with the latest SCA requirements.\n- Provide a testing environment using a fake processor to facilitate application development and testing without real financial transactions.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0078.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0078\nCREATE TABLE `billable` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `processor` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `processor_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `trial_end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `last_four_digits` char(4) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_month` int(2) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  `extra_billing_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pay_charges` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `owner_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `processor` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `processor_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `amount_refunded` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `last_four_digits` char(4) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_month` int(2) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pay_charges_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `billable` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pay_subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subscription_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `processor` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `processor_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `processor_plan` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trial_end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pay_subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `billable` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
